    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by two high-efficiency pillars: **Yordan Alvarez** (82.97) and **Christian Yelich** (75.56). **Yordan Alvarez** is our premier play, benefiting from a highly favorable matchup against E. Rodriguez (xERA 5.91) and an elite xwOBA profile that maximizes his run production potential. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** thrives in today\u2019s environment; his score is significantly bolstered by an excellent 13% dynamic platoon edge and a soft matchup against Stock (xERA 4.76). **Junior Caminero** (73.04) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (70.09) round out our top-tier options. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains a crucial engine for our stolen base objectives; while he faces a difficult platoon disadvantage against a left-handed starter, his 90% success rate against the pitcher's delivery pace and his leadoff spot make him an essential start despite the efficiency drag.\n\nIn the middle-tier, **Colt Keith** (63.94) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (61.94) offer strong production, with **Colt Keith** specifically capitalizing on a 7% platoon advantage and a favorable park factor. The most difficult decision of the day involved **Chase Meidroth**, who sits on the bench with a 48.83 score. While **Chase Meidroth** offered a slight boost from favorable wind conditions and a solid spot in the order, he ultimately fell short of the threshold set by **Dillon Dingler** (46.46) and **Carson Benge** (53.48), as our current starting outfield and middle infield depth provided more consistent baseline output. Meanwhile, **Trea Turner** (54.24) and **Kyle Schwarber** (53.43) face some risk against the tougher profile of Woo (xERA 3.59); both remain in the lineup for their category-defining ceilings, though owners should monitor their performance closely against an arm that suppresses scoring more effectively than others on today's docket. We continue to monitor the status of **Gary Sanchez**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Casey Schmitt** (IL), all of whom are unavailable for selection.",
